# Settings for the live integration suite (make integration).
# Copy this file to .integrationtests.env, which git ignores, and fill it in.
#
# It holds no tokens: those stay in your dtmgd config or the OS keyring, and
# the suite reads them through dtmgd itself. It only runs read commands
# (get, describe, query, doctor, commands) and never changes the config.

# The dtmgd config file to use (required; without it every test skips).
# Quote a path with spaces, such as macOS's "$HOME/Library/Application Support/dtmgd/config".
# DTMGD_IT_CONFIG="$HOME/.config/dtmgd/config"

# An environment context in that config (the environment tests skip without it).
# DTMGD_IT_ENV=

# A second environment context, for the --env "a;b" fan-out test (optional).
# DTMGD_IT_ENV2=staging

# A cluster context: no env-id, a Cluster API token (optional).
# DTMGD_IT_CLUSTER=prod-cluster

# An existing management zone, to check that --mz narrows the result (optional).
# DTMGD_IT_MZ=

# A log query that matches records in the time range (default: error).
# DTMGD_IT_LOG_QUERY=error

# The start of the time range for events, problems and logs (default: now-24h).
# DTMGD_IT_FROM=now-24h
